### Bug 3 root cause — the date came from the FILENAME

```python
sub["date"] = ds[4:] + ds[2:4] + ds[:2]    # DDMMYYYY -> YYYYMMDD, from the filename
```

NSE serves the PREVIOUS session's file when you request a market-holiday URL. The build stamped
that real data with a date on which nothing traded.

**Fix:** read `DATE1` from inside the file; reject any row whose internal date disagrees with the
filename. Plus `drop_duplicates` on (date, symbol) as a backstop. Rejected files are written to
`artifacts/phantom_sessions.csv` and raise a manifest warning.

**Result:**

| | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Panel sessions | 1,483 | **1,414** |
| Files rejected | — | **70** |
| Remaining phantom pairs | ~60 | **0** |
| Weekday gaps | 12 | **82** |

82 gaps over 5.7 years is correct — NSE takes 13-16 holidays a year. Per year: 14, 13, 15, 16, 13,
11. Before the fix 2021-24 showed almost none.

### Bug 2 root cause — NSE does not always adjust PREV_CLOSE on the ex-date

On KOTAKBANK's 1:5 split (14 Jan 2026) NSE printed the raw 2,132.60 beside a post-split close of
421.00, so `R = P / C.shift(1)` read 1.00 and nothing fired.

**Fix:** a second detector on the close series. A single-session fall past 35% whose inverse ratio
lands near a whole number >= 2 is a split, not a price move.

**One iteration was needed and it is worth recording.** The first attempt used a 6% tolerance and
MISSED KOTAKBANK: the observed ratio was **5.066, not 5.000**, because the stock also moved that
day. The detector now **snaps to the nearest integer** and uses that as the factor, so the residual
price move survives adjustment. Tolerance widened to 15% — the discriminator is the SIZE of the
move (NSE price bands make a real 35%+ single-session fall a corporate action), not the tolerance.

**Result:**

| | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Corporate action events | 354 | **548** (194 found via the close series) |
| Unadjusted splits market-wide | **148 across 140 symbols** | **0 across 0** |
| KOTAKBANK 13 Jan close | 2,132.60 | **426.52** |
| KOTAKBANK worst session ratio | **0.197** | **0.987** |

All 18 previously-impacted names are clean: SHILPAMED, RAMRAT, NAZARA, LALPATHLAB, BEML, MCX,
ANANDRATHI, ECLERX, PGIL, GOLDADD, CORDELIA, TDPOWERSYS, KIRLPNU, ZFCVINDIA, LICI, THYROCARE,
HDFCAMC, SMCGLOBAL.

**A correction to an earlier claim.** On 8 Sep I reported SHILPAMED at +192% over six months and
said roughly half was the split. **The true adjusted figure is +224.5% — HIGHER than I quoted.**
The old panel had the adjustment INVERTED rather than absent, so my correction was in the wrong
direction.

### One residual, knowingly accepted

**NAZARA still shows −40.5% in a single session.** Its ratio (1/0.595 = 1.68) is not near a whole
number, so the detector correctly declines to treat it as a split. It is either a non-integer
corporate action (demerger, or a 3:2 bonus) or a genuine fall. **Needs a manual check before
trusting anything computed on it.** One symbol in 3,634 is an acceptable residual.

### What this invalidates

Every historical analysis run before 26 Sep used a panel with ~140 mis-scaled symbols and 70
phantom flat sessions. That includes the 244-week Task 5 ablation, the extension cap sweep and the
stop sweep.

**They have NOT been re-run.** All three produced null results, and the contamination was ~4% of
symbols plus 70 of 1,484 sessions, so the nulls are very unlikely to flip. Re-running is roughly a
day of compute to confirm what is already concluded. **Deferred deliberately, not forgotten.**

