**The rule: a BROAD name is eligible when `dlv_adv_cr >= 10`.** Constant lives in
`build_artifacts.py` as `BROAD_DLV_ADV_FLOOR`.

**Rejected: a turnover-based size proxy.** 62% accurate against the known 500, 41% on MID. Too weak
to present as a size judgement.

**Measured effect.** Two-week daily backtest, top-10 by 3M relative strength: OLD **-0.547%/day**,
NEW **+0.821%/day**, better on 9 of 10 days. Eligible universe 240 -> 557.

**Floor set from outcomes, not exit arithmetic.** The first proposal of Rs 6cr came from "can I exit
a 15% position in two days" — the wrong question, since liquidity was never binding at this book
size. Across 33 Fridays / 11,646 observations the Rs 6-10cr band is the WORST of six (+1.43% fwd,
48% hit, negative median). Rs 10cr lifts the kept-set return from +2.74% to +3.68%.

